# kill(1)

## NAME

kill - send a signal to a process

## SYNOPSIS

    kill [-s signal | -signal] pid...
    kill -l

## DESCRIPTION

Sends a signal (default `TERM`) to the processes. The kernel has four signals: `INT` (2), `QUIT` (3), `KILL` (9) and `TERM` (15). Names may be written with or without `SIG`, in any case.

## OPTIONS

- `-s signal`: the signal to send
- `-l`: list the signal names

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `1`: an error occurred for some operand
- `2`: usage error

